## 2. Project Goals

### Short-term goals (Months 1–3)
- Finalize literature review and novelty framing.
- Stand up data ingestion pipeline (TLE retrieval, propagation, dynamic graph construction).
- Working conjunction-detection baseline (non-learned) as the comparison point.

### Long-term goals (Months 4–8)
- Trained TGNN conjunction-forecasting model beating the baseline on held-out epochs.
- Trained MARL coordination policy in simulation, evaluated against independent-agent and rule-based baselines.
- Physics-constrained optimization layer that converts policy output into feasible, fuel-costed maneuvers.

### Research goals
- A clearly stated, literature-grounded novel contribution (see Section 6.1).
- Ablations that isolate *why* the approach works (graph structure, temporal component, coordination vs. independent agents).

### Engineering goals
- A reproducible, tested, documented codebase — not a notebook collection.
- Clean separation between physics/simulation, learned models, and orchestration.

### Publication goals
- One workshop or conference submission (AIAA SciTech / IEEE Aerospace / NeurIPS-ICLR workshop track) by month 8–9.
- Figures and tables built directly from experiment-tracking outputs, not hand-drawn after the fact.

